# Scorpion Security Rules for Cursor/Claude Code

## Core Mandate

**NEVER TRUST INPUT** - All inputs (HTTP, WebSocket, LLM outputs, tool responses, webhooks) are untrusted.

## Security Checklist for All Code

When writing or reviewing Scorpion code, enforce these rules:

### 1. File Operations

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS
const filename = req.query.file;
const path = path.join('uploads', filename);
const data = await fs.readFile(path);

// ✅ ALWAYS DO THIS
import { validateFilename, resolveSafePath } from '@/lib/security';

if (!validateFilename(filename, { allowedExtensions: ['.pdf'] })) {
  return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid filename' });
}
const rootDir = path.resolve(process.cwd(), 'uploads');
const safePath = resolveSafePath(rootDir, filename);
const data = await fs.readFile(safePath);

// ✅ BEST: Use IDs, not paths
const record = await db.file.findUnique({ where: { id } });
const data = await fs.readFile(record.absolutePath);
```

### 2. Database Queries

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS
const query = `SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '${email}'`;

// ✅ ALWAYS DO THIS (parameterized)
const result = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = $1', [email]);

// ✅ OR USE ORM (Prisma)
const user = await prisma.user.findFirst({ where: { email } });
```

### 3. HTML Rendering

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS
<div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: userContent }} />

// ✅ ALWAYS DO THIS (React escapes by default)
<div>{userContent}</div>

// ✅ OR SANITIZE IF HTML IS NEEDED
import { sanitizeHtml } from '@/lib/security/sanitize';
<div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{
  __html: sanitizeHtml(userContent, { allowedTags: ['p', 'strong', 'em'] })
}} />
```

### 4. API Routes

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS
export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  const body = await request.json();
  // No validation!
}

// ✅ ALWAYS DO THIS
import { withSecurity } from '@/lib/security/middleware';
import { z } from 'zod';

const schema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1).max(100),
  email: z.string().email(),
});

export const POST = withSecurity(
  {
    bodySchema: schema,
    rateLimit: { windowMs: 60000, maxRequests: 100 },
  },
  async (request: NextRequest) => {
    const body = await request.json(); // Already validated
    // ... handler logic
  }
);
```

### 5. Tool Execution (LLM/Agent)

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS
const result = await exec(agentCommand);

// ✅ ALWAYS DO THIS
import { validateToolCall } from '@/lib/security';

const validation = validateToolCall({
  name: 'executeShell',
  args: { command: agentCommand },
});

if (!validation.safe) {
  throw new Error(`Blocked: ${validation.reason}`);
}
const result = await exec(agentCommand);
```

### 6. Chat Messages

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS
await db.message.create({ data: { content: userMessage } });

// ✅ ALWAYS DO THIS
import { sanitizeChatMessage } from '@/lib/security/sanitize';

const sanitized = sanitizeChatMessage(userMessage);
await db.message.create({ data: { content: sanitized } });
```

